Make the group kill-XP rate independent of party level spread.

Touches: src/server/game/Entities/Player/KillRewarder.cpp,
KillRewarder::_RewardPlayer

Why: report #107 / GitHub issue #105 -- "everyone in a party gets the
highest member's XP bonus and no low-level grouping penalty."

Upstream, a grouped member's kill-XP rate is

  _groupRate * playerLevel / aliveSumLevel

where _groupRate is xp_in_group_rate(count, isRaid). The second factor is
the classic low-level grouping penalty: the bigger the level gap between
you and the rest of the party, the smaller your share, so a high level
character grouping with low level friends (or playerbots) earns a
fraction of their kill XP.

With LivingGear.PartyXp.NoLowLevelPenalty (default ON, declared in
living_gear.conf.dist) the factor is fixed at 1.0: every member earns
the plain group size rate. Nothing else changes -- the victim's grey
cutoff (_maxNotGrayMember / _isFullXP half-XP) is untouched,
xp_in_group_rate still shrinks the rate by party size, and the
config-off path reproduces the original formula exactly. Quest XP does
not pass through KillRewarder and is unaffected.

The "highest member's XP bonus" half of #107 lives in the module
(LivingGear_Progression.cpp, LivingGear.PartyXp.EqualBonus): Bonesaw's
personal XP bonuses are applied per player in OnPlayerGiveXP, where each
member's own bonus is what the hook can see, so the module walks the
group and applies the maximum member multiplier to everyone. Kill XP
only -- OnPlayerGiveXP never fires for quest XP.

Config keys live in modules/mod-living-gear/conf/living_gear.conf.dist;
the core reads them through sConfigMgr like any other conf property.

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Player/KillRewarder.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Player/KillRewarder.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
  */
 
 #include "KillRewarder.h"
+#include "Config.h"
 #include "Creature.h"
 #include "Formulas.h"
 #include "Group.h"
@@ -223,7 +224,19 @@
     // Give reputation and kill credit only in PvE.
     if (!_isPvP || _isBattleGround)
     {
-        float xpRate = _group ? _groupRate * float(_GetPlayerLevel(player)) / _aliveSumLevel : /*Personal rate is 100%.*/ 1.0f; // Group rate depends on the sum of levels.
+        // [Bonesaw #107] Party XP: the engine's level-share factor
+        // (level / aliveSumLevel) penalised anyone grouped with lower-level
+        // players. With LivingGear.PartyXp.NoLowLevelPenalty (default on) the
+        // factor is always 1.0, so every member earns the plain group size
+        // rate (xp_in_group_rate); the victim's grey cutoff is untouched.
+        float xpRate;
+        if (_group)
+        {
+            static bool const noLevelSharePenalty = sConfigMgr->GetOption<bool>("LivingGear.PartyXp.NoLowLevelPenalty", true);
+            xpRate = _groupRate * (noLevelSharePenalty ? 1.0f : float(_GetPlayerLevel(player)) / _aliveSumLevel);
+        }
+        else
+            xpRate = 1.0f; // Personal rate is 100%.
         sScriptMgr->OnPlayerRewardKillRewarder(player, this, isDungeon, xpRate);                                                // Personal rate is 100%.
 
         if (_xp)
